Why GPL, when the code this forked was permissive

OpenHub is a hard fork of OpenLogi, which is dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0.
This project ships the device illustrations from Piper (below), which are
GPL-2.0-or-later, and combining copyleft artwork into a distributed work makes
the whole work copyleft. That was a deliberate trade: accurate illustrations of
76 devices, with their button anchor points already placed, in exchange for
copyleft.

The inherited OpenLogi code remains available under its own MIT/Apache-2.0
terms from upstream. Relicensing a combined work does not, and cannot,
retroactively change the licence of anyone else's contribution — it only states
the terms under which this combination is distributed.

